From 15f382fe1005061aad6e2c7c1372303baa05bc94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:33:56 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/33] Assemble: let the mdadm that starts an array set its
 resync point

With incremental assembly (mdadm -I per disk, run by udev in parallel at
boot) the member array of a container is set up by the first mdadm that
sees it, with the resync point its disks gave then, and started by the one
that has enough disks.  assemble_container_content() calls
sysfs_set_array() only when the array is not set up yet, so md starts it
with what the first mdadm knew.

That is fine when every member carries the same metadata (IMSM, DDF).  It
is not when the metadata is not on every member: AMD RAIDXpert2 keeps its
write-intent bitmap on one member only.  If that disk comes last, the
first mdadm cannot read the bitmap and either takes a clean array for
dirty (a needless full resync after every reboot, seen with RAID10 on real
disks) or, worse, takes an array that crashed for clean, and its mirrors
are never resynced.

When the array was set up before, write the resync point of the starting
mdadm (it has the fuller view) before starting the array.  --force still
has the last word.  For formats with the metadata on every member the
value written is the same as before.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
---
 Assemble.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Assemble.c b/Assemble.c
index 3829e984..fe6d1aad 100644
--- a/Assemble.c
+++ b/Assemble.c
@@ -2009,6 +2009,7 @@ int assemble_container_content(struct supertype *st, int mdfd,
 	int err;
 	int is_clean, all_disks;
 	bool is_raid456;
+	bool set_up_before = false;
 
 	if (sysfs_init(content, mdfd, NULL)) {
 		pr_err("Unable to initialize sysfs\n");
@@ -2029,6 +2030,8 @@ int assemble_container_content(struct supertype *st, int mdfd,
 			sysfs_free(sra);
 			return 1;
 		}
+	} else {
+		set_up_before = true;
 	}
 
 	/* There are two types of reshape: container wide or sub-array specific
@@ -2174,6 +2177,17 @@ int assemble_container_content(struct supertype *st, int mdfd,
 		return 1;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Incremental assembly: the array was set up by the mdadm that saw
+	 * it first, with the resync point the disks it had then gave.  Where
+	 * the metadata is not on every member (AMD keeps its write-intent
+	 * bitmap on one), the mdadm that starts the array has the fuller
+	 * view: its resync point is the one md starts with.
+	 */
+	if (set_up_before &&
+	    sysfs_set_num(content, NULL, "resync_start", content->resync_start))
+		return 1;
+
 	if (is_raid456 && content->resync_start != MaxSector && c->force &&
 	    all_disks < content->array.raid_disks) {
 
